- Legacy Vundle patching flow unless you keep old Vim path.

Maintenance:
   - Keeping README.WSL and Agent in Sync:
    README.WSL is the source of truth for WSL setup.
    Update agents/WSL_DEV_SETUP/agent.md in the same change when setup
    steps change.
    No sync script is used or maintained.

    1. Edit README.WSL with your changes.
    2. Update agents/WSL_DEV_SETUP/agent.md manually to match.
    3. Review both files together with git diff.
    4. Commit both files together.

   - Agent Usage:
     In VS Code Copilot chat, invoke the agent with:
        @wsl_dev_setup Please help me set up WSL
     
     Agent will guide you through each step interactively.
     Logs saved to: ~/access-UK/.wsl_setup_logs/wsl_setup.<timestamp>.log

Coverage checklist from old README:
- SSH clone, Vim, Bash, Zsh, netrc/screen/inputrc/gdbinit, git, tmux.
- Docs-UK, Solarized/dircolors, percol->fzf, xsel, asciidoc.
- diffconflicts, mosh, executable bits, noip, Unite/vimproc, fonts.
- Neovim (uday config + NvChad path), fugitive/git version.
- samba/vnc/desktop/display guidance, python, copilot CLI, claude.
- pwd.sh / WS helper and ALU-related notes.
